                             4. ENFORCEMENT

The copyright holder actively monitors for infringement and WILL act on it.

Infringing copies will be met with DMCA takedown notices filed against the
infringing listing and, where warranted, the infringer's host, payment
processor and platform account. GitHub, Gumroad, Itch.io, Patreon, Ko-fi,
Etsy, Shopify, Discord, YouTube and Twitch all honour these, and repeat
notices against the same account lead to its termination under their
respective repeat-infringer policies.

Where the infringement is commercial or willful, the copyright holder will
pursue the full remedies available under the United States Copyright Act
(17 U.S.C. § 501 et seq.), which may include injunctive relief, the
infringer's profits, actual damages, and - where the work is registered -
statutory damages of up to $150,000 per work willfully infringed, plus
costs and attorney's fees under 17 U.S.C. § 505.

Note the words "per work" in section 1(b). The twenty-one characters are
not one asset.

Infringement is easy to prove here and hard to argue away. This repository
carries a complete, timestamped commit history recording every sprite from
its first pixel, and the artwork is original rather than adapted - there is
no prior art to hide behind and no "we both used the same asset pack"
defence available.

